===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} Anything old or of inferior quality.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Jim Dwyer (journalist)|Jim Dwyer]]|title=More Awesome Than Money|quotee={{w|Eben Moglen}}|year=2014|publisher=Viking|page=26–27|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/moreawesomethanm0000dwye/page/26/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-670-02560-2|passage=Students “still think of privacy as ‘the one secret I don’t want revealed,’ and that’s not the problem. Their problem is all the stuff that’s the '''cruft''', the data dandruff, of life, that they don’t think of as secret in any way, but which aggregates to stuff that they don't want anybody to know,” Moglen said.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2020|work=The Washington Post|passage=The document just goes on at length in the same way, picking out the sort of '''cruft''' that’s been littering Trump’s Twitter feed since Nov. 3 and tying it all into one stinky package. It’s sincerely not worth running through the entire litany again; simply consider ''The Post''’s Fact Checker articles as an effective rejoinder.}}
# {{lb|en|computing|slang}} Redundant, old or improperly written [[code]], especially that which accumulates over time.
#: {{syn|en|clutter}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Andrew S. Tanenbaum|title={{w|Modern Operating Systems}}|year=2015|isbn=978-0-13-359162-0|origyear=1992|page=908|edition=4th|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/modern-operating-systems-2015/page/908/mode/1up|passage=The PEB includes the list of loaded modules (i.e., the EXE and DLLs), the memory containing environment strings, the current working directory, and data for managing the process’ heaps—as well as lots of special-case Win32 '''cruft''' that has been added over time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Shelley Powers|title=JavaScript Cookbook|year=2015|location=Sebastopol|publisher=O'Reilly|page=143|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/isbn_9781491901885/page/143/mode/1up|isbn=9781491901885|passage=Best developer practices run the gamut from keeping the '''cruft''' out of your code to ensuring your code is accessible to all your application or site’s users.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2021/08/the-perl-foundation-is-fragmenting-over-code-of-conduct-enforcement/|title=The Perl Foundation is fragmenting over Code of Conduct enforcement|date=2021-08-14|author=Jim Salter|quotee=Sawyer X|work=Ars Technica|passage=Sawyer cites responses to a message saying "there is '''cruft''' in [Perl]" as the excuse some Perl community members used to "push him into a corner" until he deactivated his Twitter account.}}
# {{lb|en|film|slang}} Meaningless and/or gratuitous content displayed on computer consoles in visual entertainment productions.

